        <groundspeak:log id="1253422214">
          <groundspeak:date>2024-08-14T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="25790230">MaybeSunshine</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP745 HFHR Water Tower [FOUND]&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Somewhat battered, but found in about 2 seconds, which is surely not what I expected after reading the last log. TFTCap.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="980802787">
          <groundspeak:date>2020-11-21T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Write note</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="181446">DanOCan</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP745 - HFHR Water Tower&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Failed to locate this one.  I reviewed previous logs while on site and found Mr. Canoehead's photo from September of 2016 which provided some of the best context and it looks like the sidewalk was reconfigured to add a wheelchair cutout and the spot where the cap was located may now be under concrete.  A lot can change in the 3+ years since anyone last logged this one.  Or, I may have just missed it -- I know it has happened before.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="703177437">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-07-19T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="1685537">nosweat6060</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP745 HFHR Water Tower [FOUND]

This was my third HR cap today. I am getting better at spotting them but sometimes they are hidden in plain sight. I have the numbers and will try to add a photo later. Thanks for efforts at keeping this going - I really like this addition to my geocaching activities.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="684684029">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-07T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="3061435">Iron Phoenix</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP745 - HFHR Water Tower&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Out for yet another day of capping and caching with OBA, this time in Lethbridge!! &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile_big.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt; Along the way there and back. &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile_wink.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt; A bit of a chunk taken out of the cap and a few scars on it, but the weird part was the water tower. Where did it go? &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile_shock.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt; TFTCap!!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
